---
/* A US route into existing formation guides, not duplicated coaching advice. */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Coaching in the USA' }];
const formats = [
  { age: 'U7–U8', size: '4v4', note: 'US Soccer recommends up to 4v4. We do not yet cover this format.' },
  { age: 'U9–U10', size: '7v7', note: 'Starting shapes, simple playing principles and player responsibilities.', href: '/formations/7v7/' },
  { age: 'U11–U12', size: '9v9', note: 'Complete formation playbooks, tactical diagrams and positional roles.', href: '/formations/9v9/' },
  { age: 'U13+', size: '11v11', note: 'The next stage of the pathway. We do not currently cover 11v11.' }
];
---
<Base title="Youth Soccer Formations: 7v7 & 9v9 Guides | How We Play" description="Free 7v7 and 9v9 soccer formation guides for US youth and rec soccer coaches. Simple tactics, player positions and printable PDFs for U9–U12 teams." lang="en-US" ogLocale="en_US" crumbs={crumbs} ogType="website" editorial meta={{ type: 'guide', group: 'US coaches' }}>
  <header class="page-head ed-grid usa-head"><div class="page-head__text"><p class="ed-kicker">For coaches in the United States</p><h1>Soccer, football. Same game.</h1><p class="ed-stand">Our free formation guides come from an English grassroots touchline. Here's how to find the right one for your US youth soccer team.</p></div><aside class="usa-head__note"><p class="ed-label">Start with the format</p><p>Choose by the number of players on the field rather than age alone. Youth soccer formats can vary between leagues and competitions.</p></aside></header>

  <section class="ed-section ed-grid usa-pathway" aria-labelledby="usa-pathway-h"><div class="usa-pathway__heading"><p class="ed-kicker">US Soccer pathway</p><h2 class="ed-h2" id="usa-pathway-h">Find your team's format</h2><p class="ed-small">These are US Soccer's recommended maximum game formats. Check your local league's rules.</p></div><ol class="usa-pathway__grid">{formats.map(item => <li class:list={['usa-pathway__card', { 'usa-pathway__card--available': !!item.href }]}><p class="usa-pathway__age">{item.age}</p><h3>{item.size}</h3><p>{item.note}</p>{item.href ? <a href={item.href}>Explore {item.size} guides <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> : <span class="usa-pathway__pending">Not covered yet</span>}</li>)}</ol></section>

  <section class="ed-section ed-grid split usa-rec" aria-labelledby="usa-rec-h">
    <div class="split__main">
      <p class="ed-kicker">For volunteer and parent coaches</p>
      <h2 class="ed-h2" id="usa-rec-h">Coaching rec soccer? Start here.</h2>
      <p class="ed-lede">Recreational soccer, often called rec soccer, is community-based youth soccer with an emphasis on participation, enjoyment and development.</p>
      <p class="ed-small">What's the best formation for a rec soccer team? There isn't one best shape for everyone. Our guides give you a starting shape, four playing principles and clear player responsibilities that you can adapt to your team. They're practical coaching ideas, not official league instructions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split__side usa-rec__cta">
      <p class="ed-label">Free formation guides</p>
      <a class="ed-btn" href="/formations/7v7/2-3-1/">2-3-1 formation · 7v7 soccer →</a>
      <a class="ed-btn" href="/formations/9v9/3-1-3-1/">3-1-3-1 formation · 9v9 soccer →</a>
      <p class="ed-small">Start with the format your league plays. Age groups and local rules can vary.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ed-section ed-grid split usa-compare" aria-labelledby="usa-compare-h"><div class="split__main"><p class="ed-kicker">Why the ages look different</p><h2 class="ed-h2" id="usa-compare-h">One format. Different ages.</h2><p class="ed-lede">England introduced new youth football formats for 2026/27. The US pathway is different, but the ideas in our 7v7 and 9v9 guides still apply.</p><p class="ed-small">We use English football terms. In the US, football is soccer and a pitch is a field. The on-field decisions don't change with the wording.</p></div><div class="split__side"><table class="usa-compare__table"><caption>Typical age groups by format, 2026/27</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Format</th><th scope="col">USA</th><th scope="col">England</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">7v7</th><td>U9–U10</td><td>U10–U11</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9v9</th><td>U11–U12</td><td>U12–U13</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="ed-small">Age groups are a guide, not a substitute for your competition's rules.</p></div></section>

  <section class="ed-section ed-grid split usa-story" aria-labelledby="usa-story-h"><div class="split__main"><p class="ed-kicker">From the grassroots touchline</p><h2 class="ed-h2" id="usa-story-h">Made by a coach, for coaches.</h2><p class="ed-lede">How We Play Football grew from seven years coaching youth teams in England: league wins, heavy defeats and players earning trials with Premier League clubs.</p><p class="ed-small">These aren't official academy programmes or instructions from professional clubs. They're practical starting points for volunteer coaches to adapt to their teams.</p><p><a class="ed-go" href="/about/">Read our story →</a></p></div><div class="split__side usa-story__cta"><p class="ed-label">Ready to explore?</p><a class="ed-btn" href="/formations/7v7/">7v7 soccer guides →</a><a class="ed-btn" href="/formations/9v9/">9v9 soccer guides →</a></div></section>

  <section class="ed-section ed-grid usa-sources" aria-labelledby="usa-sources-h"><div><h2 class="ed-h3" id="usa-sources-h">Guidance and sources</h2><p class="ed-small">Formats reflect <a href="https://www.ussoccer.com/us-way/player-development/game/game-formats" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">US Soccer's recommendations</a> and <a href="https://www.englandfootball.com/play/youth-football/Youth-Club-Football" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">England Football's youth pathway</a> for 2026/27. <a href="https://usclubsoccer.org/programs/leagues/recreation-community/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">US Club Soccer</a> describes rec programs as primarily local, in-house or community leagues. US Youth Soccer, US Club Soccer and AYSO introduced an August–July age-group registration cycle from 2026/27. See <a href="https://www.ussoccer.com/ecosystem-review/player-registration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">US Soccer's registration guidance</a>. Always confirm your competition's rules.</p></div></section>
</Base>
